<rml>
<head>
	<title>Generic Confirm Dialog Background</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="base.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="generic_confirm_dialog_bg.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/template" href="window_shell_bg.rml"/>
</head>
<!-- Background-context document (see npc_shop_bg.rml for the mechanism) -- paints the panel's own
     frame/fill BEFORE the 3D pass draws item3D each frame, so the item shows through the gap in
     generic_confirm_dialog.rml's own now-paint-less #panel instead of being painted over by it. No
     data-model -- #panel centers via plain CSS, unlike npc_shop_bg's own root_x/root_y/root_scale
     data-style bindings: this dialog's position is never C++-computed.

     Shell structure (edge/groove/content slot) now lives in window_shell_bg.rml -- see its own
     comment for why #panel doesn't get .modern-frame here (this dialog's own bespoke hatched-iron
     paint stays in generic_confirm_dialog_bg.rcss, targeting #panel/#content directly), and for why
     base.rcss is linked directly HERE rather than from within the template (token(...) substitution
     only applies to a document's own direct rcss links, not to anything a linked template brings
     in). -->
<body template="window_shell_bg"></body>
</rml>
